# Drag a foot window by its title bar to the left edge.
setup foot &
wait 2
ptr move 960 540 sleep 100 glide 960 60 200 down glide 2 540 400 sleep 500
shot snap-left
note Drag held at the left edge: the preview shows the left half of the screen (translucent, same as QML in this look).
rec snap-corner 0.8 ptr move 960 540 glide 960 60 200 down glide 2 540 400 sleep 500 glide 2 2 300 sleep 500
note Gliding to the top-left corner moves the preview to the top-left quarter over 200 ms; compare the move with QML within 1 frame.
ptr move 960 540 glide 960 60 200 down glide 2 540 400 sleep 300 up
wait 1
shot snap-release
note After release the preview fades out in 100 ms; the window is tiled to the left half.
# alternative: ipc qs ipc call tiling snap left (QML only); not run
setup pkill -x foot || true
